WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:00.923
- All right, everybody.

00:00:00.923 --> 00:00:03.370
Let's wrap up with one
last feel good story

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.760
from the feeds of social media.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:05.841
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.841 --> 00:00:06.674
(Upbeat music)

00:00:06.674 --> 00:00:09.040
(Audience clapping)

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.930
Every weekend a North
Carolina couple serves up

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:14.330
a Sunday Funday feast for their neighbors.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.400
These are seriously awesome
meals like Carolina dogs with

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.640
homemade chili,

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.200
barbecue chicken sandwiches
with crunchy slop

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.754
and vegetarian rigatoni for the others.

00:00:25.754 --> 00:00:26.587
(Laughs)

00:00:26.587 --> 00:00:29.810
And get this the dish out, all
these amazing meals for free.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:31.760
That's incredible. There's only one catch.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.210
There's no takeout people that's

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.760
because chefs Joey and
Scott want you to stay

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.910
and connect with the
community, which is super cool.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:40.756
We have Joey and Scott
dialed in from Charlotte.

00:00:40.756 --> 00:00:41.589
(Audience Applause)
They watch weekdays

00:00:41.589 --> 00:00:42.639
at 5P, WCCB show ,CW.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:45.373
So Joey,

00:00:46.914 --> 00:00:49.390
I'll start with you. How
did this all get started?

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:52.580
- Well we opened the
NoDa, our Company Store

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:53.413
in our neighborhood.

00:00:53.413 --> 00:00:55.460
It's a funky little
eclectic neighborhood here

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.460
in Charlotte, North Carolina.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:02.090
We opened it in the spring
of 2016 and one weekend.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:02.923
It was a beautiful day.

00:01:02.923 --> 00:01:06.030
It was a beautiful Sunday
and we both had to work

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:07.500
and we loved to barbecue.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.260
And so we decided to just
roll our grill from our house,

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:14.350
up to the store and cook
out a few hamburgers.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:17.500
I think we serve maybe 10
or 15 people at that point.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.880
And we enjoyed the conversation so much

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:20.960
and getting to know our neighbors,

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.575
that we decided to do it
again the following week and

00:01:24.575 --> 00:01:25.408
- The following week.

00:01:25.408 --> 00:01:26.820
- Yep, and the following week.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.830
And so fast forward five years,

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:31.040
and we've been doing it every week.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:34.830
Now we serve about 150 to
200 plates. And of course,

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:35.663
Scott and I,

00:01:35.663 --> 00:01:38.490
have gotten to meet a ton
of wonderful people as well.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:39.500
- That amazing.
(Audience Claps)

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.470
It's such a cool thing you're doing,

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:43.650
but Scott, you don't
just do burgers and dogs.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.310
These meals are super elaborate, right?

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:49.670
- Right. We love to get
inspired by different things,

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:50.720
different foods we're trying.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:52.500
And so we'll do some things like Kimchi,

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.710
which is something that
specialists have to ferment for a

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.769
couple of weeks. If not more,

00:01:56.769 --> 00:01:58.920
we've done marinated flank steak tacos,

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.160
where the meat has to
marinate for a few days,

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:06.023
leading up to the meal, we make
our own homemade hot sauces.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.410
And so it, it, you know, we,

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:11.550
we put in a lot of time and
effort and everything into this,

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:12.820
but we love to cook.

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:16.190
And we really love seeing
strangers become friends

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:17.610
within our community.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.900
And it's even been so much so that,

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:21.960
we know of at least two couples that met

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.340
at a Sunday Funday free lunch.

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.297
They're now married.

00:02:24.297 --> 00:02:25.130
(Audience Applause)

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:27.680
And then we also had (Indistinct)

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.130
at a Sunday Funday that asked us,

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:31.606
if they could have their wedding sort of

00:02:31.606 --> 00:02:34.810
at our store set up as a
Sunday Funday free lunch,

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:36.320
where they invited the whole neighborhood

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:39.150
and provided food to anyone
that wanted to show up

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:39.983
for their wedding.

00:02:39.983 --> 00:02:41.289
And it was packed. It was wonderful.

00:02:41.289 --> 00:02:42.428
(Audience clapping)

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.350
It's, it's something fun.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.183
I mean, we're,

00:02:44.183 --> 00:02:45.016
we're trying to create community

00:02:45.016 --> 00:02:46.860
and we're literally
helping create families.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.210
- I love that. Just bringing
the community together.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.043
And I,

00:02:50.043 --> 00:02:51.800
I love that it's not takeout
and people kind of have to sit

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:53.220
and hang that's. That's really cool.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.210
I think especially people are
craving it right now as well.

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:57.240
For the last two years
we've been like so isolated.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.030
So it's such a cool thing
to be able to do and get out

00:02:59.030 --> 00:02:59.863
and just, (Audience clapping)

00:02:59.863 --> 00:03:01.260
you know, interact with people.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.270
Well, thank you so much, Joey and Scott,

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:05.090
I'm liking your post right now

00:03:07.569 --> 00:03:08.740
and that's not all,

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.740
our season long partner
Pilot Pen that goes

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:11.890
deep into the Kelly Clarkson show,

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:14.410
likes to celebrate those
who create fearlessly,

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:15.330
just like y'all.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:17.350
So they're going to be using
their friction erasable pen

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:19.457
to write you a check $4000.

00:03:19.457 --> 00:03:21.096
(Audience clapping)
How does that sounds?

00:03:21.096 --> 00:03:22.518
(Laughs)

00:03:22.518 --> 00:03:24.701
- That's insane, thank you so much.

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:25.692
- That's a great reaction.

00:03:25.692 --> 00:03:27.630
(Laughs)

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:29.630
Well thank you all so much , keep it up.

